  (1-\lambda) x$. We distinguish two cases. First, assume~$p^* \in
  V$. Then~$z(\lambda) \in V$ for every~${\lambda \in [0,1]}$ and, due
  to (i) in Definition ef{DEDA}, there is~${c_{\lambda} \in  ar{C}}$
  with~${
orm{z(\lambda)-c_{\lambda}} \leq
    \varepsilon}$. If~$
orm{p^*-x} \leq \varepsilon$ then
  \[ 
orm{p^*-c^*} \leq 
orm{p^*-c_0} \leq 
orm{p^*-x} +

orm{x-c_0} \leq 2\varepsilon. \] If~$
orm{p^*-x} > \varepsilon$,
  set ${\lambda}^* =  rac{\varepsilon}{
orm{p^*-x}}$. Similarly, we
  have
  \[ 
orm{p^*-c^*} \leq 
orm{p^*-c_{{\lambda}^*}} \leq

orm{p^*-z({\lambda}^*)} + 
orm{z({\lambda}^*)-c_{{\lambda}^*}} \leq
    2\varepsilon. \] Now, assume~${p^* 
otin V}$. Then there
  exists~$ ar{\lambda} \in (0,1)$, such that~$z( ar{\lambda}) \in V$
  and~$z(\lambda) 
otin V$ for all $\lambda \in
  ( ar{\lambda},1]$. For~${\lambda \in ( ar{\lambda},1]}$,
  $z(\lambda)$ can be written as ${z(\lambda) = v_{\lambda} +
    t_{\lambda}d_{\lambda}}$ with $v_{\lambda} = \argmin \{

orm{z( ar{\lambda}) - v} \;\mid\;$ $v \in \left(\{z(\lambda)\} -
        ecc{P}ight) \cap V \}$, $t_{\lambda} \geq 0$ and
  $d_{\lambda} \in ecc{P}$, $
orm{d_{\lambda}} = 1$. By the
  definition of $\ed$-approximation there exist~$c_{\lambda} \in C$
  and~$ ar{d_{\lambda}} \in ecc{C}$ such
  that~$
orm{v_{\lambda}-c_{\lambda}} \leq \varepsilon$
  and~$
orm{d_{\lambda}- ar{d_{\lambda}}} \leq \delta$. Now we have
   egin{equation}\label{proof_PHDA_1}

orm{z(\lambda) - (c_{\lambda} + t_{\lambda} ar{d_{\lambda}})} \leq

orm{v_{\lambda}-c_{\lambda}} + t_{\lambda}

orm{d_{\lambda}- ar{d_{\lambda}}} \leq \varepsilon +
    t_{\lambda}\delta.
  \end{equation}
  Furthermore, $t_{\lambda} =

orm{z(\lambda)-v_{\lambda}}$, because $
orm{d_{\lambda}} =
  1$. Hence,
   egin{equation}\label{proof_PHDA_2}
     egin{aligned} t_{\lambda} &\leq

orm{z(\lambda)-z( ar{\lambda})} + 
orm{z( ar{\lambda}) -
        v_{\lambda}} \leq 
orm{z(\lambda)-z( ar{\lambda})} +

orm{z( ar{\lambda})-v_1} \ &\leq

orm{z(\lambda)-z( ar{\lambda})} + 
orm{z( ar{\lambda})-x} +

orm{x -v_1} \ &= 
