  \in ecc{C}$. Therefore let $c \in C$, $t \geq 0$ and define $y^{
u} =
  \argmin_{y \in C} 
orm{v^{
u}-y}$. By the triangle inequality it
  holds true, that
   egin{equation}\label{proof_LBS}

orm{c-r^{
u}-y^{
u}} \leq M + 
orm{c-x} +

orm{v^{
u}-y^{
u}} =: \ols{M}^{
u}.
  \end{equation}
  Note, that $\ols{M}^{
u}$ is bounded from above by some $\ols{M}$, because
  $
orm{v^{
u}-y^{
u}} ightarrow 0$. For every $T \geq 0$ there
  exists some $
u_T$, such that $
orm{r^{
u_T}} \geq T$. Let $T
  \geq t$ and define
  \[  ar{y} :=  rac{t}{
orm{r^{
u_T}}} y^{
u_T} + \left(
      1- rac{t}{
orm{r^{
u_T}}} ight) c \in C. \]
  Putting it all together one gets
   egin{equation*}
     egin{aligned}
      \inf_{y \in C} 
orm{(c-td^{
u_T})-y} &\leq

orm{(c-td^{
u_T})- ar{y}} \
