 egin{proposition}\label{PEP}
  Let $C \subseteq \R^n$ be nonempty closed convex and
  line-free. For $
u \in \mathbb{N}$ let~$P^{
u}$ be an
  $(\varepsilon^{
u},\delta^{
u})$-approximation of
  $C$. If~${(\varepsilon^{
u},\delta^{
u}) ightarrow (0,0)}$, then
  for every extreme point~$c$ of $C$ there exists a sequence~${x^{
u}
    ightarrow c}$ such that $x^{
u} \in \conv \vertices P^{
u}$.
